<title>USA: Freuhauf Trailer asset sale to Wabash cleared.</title>
<headline>Freuhauf Trailer asset sale to Wabash cleared.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS, Ind. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fruehauf Trailer Corp said Wednesday the U.S. Bankruptcy Court in the District of Delaware approved the previously announced sale of assets to Wabash National Corp for about $52 million.</p>
<p>Fruehauf said the sale includes its Fort Madison, Iowa, and Scott County, Tenn., manufacturing facilities; sales and distribution business consisting of 31 retail outlets; aftermarket parts distribution business based in Grove City, Ohio; and all trademarks and patents including the Fruehauf name.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to close the sale after receiving regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
